preConditionHook:
// THE META-FILTER: a reversal signal AT A LEVEL is worth more than the same
// signal in open space. The close is within magnetToleranceAtr ATRs of ANY of
// the corpus's mechanized magnets -- the lookback-bar high above, the
// lookback-bar low below, or the EMA.
//
// DELIBERATELY A COMPOSITE, against the usual "atomic beats composite" rule,
// because ENTRY PANES AND. TouchOfRecentExtreme AND CloseWithinAtrOfEma requires
// BOTH to be true, which is not what Brooks means -- he means any ONE of them.
// That OR is unreachable from the parts, so it is a rule; DayOfWeekAnyOf exists
// in the catalog for exactly this reason.
//
// THE ROUND-NUMBER TERM OF THE MERGED RULE IS NOT WRITTEN. Distance to the
// nearest multiple of a step needs a rounding word -- Round, IntPortion, Floor
// or Mod -- and NONE of them has a VERIFIED or ACCEPTED row in EL_FEATURES.md
// (Mod's row is UNKNOWN), so there is no register-clean way to spell it. The
// remaining three magnets are written; the round-number disjunct can be added
// later as another OR term, exactly as the merge notes anticipate for trend
// lines, channel lines and measured-move targets. roundStep is therefore not an
// input.
//
// THE EXTREMES EXCLUDE BAR 0 -- the twin takes its highest over the
// one-bar-shifted price series rather than lagging the function's own result,
// which would be a function-history reference the register does not cover -- so this bar's own high cannot be the
// level it is being measured against. The loop here mirrors that, seeded from
// bar 1 and running to bar lookback.
//
// IDENTICAL BOTH SIDES: the test is a distance, measured with std::fabs (EL's
// AbsValue), and carries no direction.
//
// MultiWalk's WFSafe_AvgTrueRange is the ROLLING accumulator of AtrProfitTarget,
// two separate accumulator statements and a re-seed on a length change.
// WFSafe_Xaverage is MEASURED bit-identical to plain XAverage at a fixed length,
// seeded with the PRICE on the study's first calculated bar, recurrence
// x + sf*(p - x) as ONE statement, no warm-up hole; the walkforward LENGTH
// CHANGE is still unmeasured, so PIN emaLength in the grid. Only the CURRENT
// EMA is read -- the lagged read XAverage(...)[k] remains unmeasured and no
// rule here depends on it.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope
// declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: max(lookback, atrLookback + 1).
if (atrLenState != (int)atrLookback) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (aa = 0; aa < (int)atrLookback; ++aa) {
        hiV = high[aa] > close[aa + 1] ? high[aa] : close[aa + 1];
        loV = low[aa] < close[aa + 1] ? low[aa] : close[aa + 1];
        atrSum += hiV - loV;
    }
    atrLenState = (int)atrLookback;
} else {
    outIdx = (int)atrLookback;
    hiV = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    loV = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    hiO = high[outIdx] > close[outIdx + 1] ? high[outIdx] : close[outIdx + 1];
    loO = low[outIdx] < close[outIdx + 1] ? low[outIdx] : close[outIdx + 1];
    atrSum += hiV - loV;
    atrSum -= hiO - loO;
}
atrValue = atrSum / (int)atrLookback;
emaSf = 2.0 / (emaLength + 1.0);
if (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1) {
    emaVal = close[0];
} else {
    emaVal = emaVal + emaSf * (close[0] - emaVal);
}
hh = high[1];
ll = low[1];
for (kk = 1; kk <= (int)lookback; ++kk) {
    if (el_gt(high[kk], hh)) hh = high[kk];
    if (el_lt(low[kk], ll)) ll = low[kk];
}
tol = magnetToleranceAtr * atrValue;
